# nr-relay-smtp: the SMTP client and MIME builder in mixdog-relay/src/mail (replace nodemailer)

No new crate and no protocol row. One dependency edge of the crate itself (md-5, for AUTH CRAM-MD5 with the hmac the
crate already has) and two test targets that need the feature `test-support` (the test-only root of the fake servers).
The source is written for these edits; nothing was compiled here.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml

In [dependencies], between the lines `httparse = { workspace = true }` and `mixdog-fsio = { workspace = true }`, add:

    md-5 = { workspace = true }

(`md-5 = "0.10.6"` is already in [workspace.dependencies] of native/core/Cargo.toml; the library name is `md5`, so the
code says `md5::Md5`.)

After the existing `[[test]] name = "twin"` block, add:

    [[test]]
    name = "smtp"
    path = "tests/smtp.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

    [[test]]
    name = "smtp_twin"
    path = "tests/smtp_twin.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

(`mail::send_trusting`, which the two tests call, is compiled for `any(test, feature = "test-support")`; an integration
test is built without `cfg(test)` on the library, so it needs the feature.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock

In the `[[package]] name = "mixdog-relay"` dependencies array add `"md-5 0.10.6",` between `"libc",` and
`"mixdog-fsio",` (the array is sorted; two md-5 versions are locked, 0.10.6 is the one `[workspace.dependencies]`
names). The build is --locked: without this line it fails. Nothing else in the lock changes (md-5 0.10.6 and its
digest dependencies are already locked and compiled for mixdog-pdf-codec).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Regenerate with the project's hakari command if it reports a difference for md-5 (no new feature set is asked for: the
default features of md-5 0.10.6 are the ones mixdog-pdf-codec already builds).

## mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING

Nothing: no protocol method belongs to this task.

## What the feedback task consumes

`mixdog_relay::mail::{send, MailConfig, MailError, MailCode, Message, Attachment}`:

    MailConfig::new(host, port, user, pass)       // timeout 15 s, secure = (port == 465)
    send(&MailConfig, &Message) -> Result<(), MailError>   // async; MailError.code.as_str() is the logged code
    Message { from, to, reply_to: Option<String>, subject, text, attachments: Vec<Attachment>, message_id: Option<String> }
    Attachment { filename, content: Vec<u8> (decoded bytes, not base64), content_type }   // disposition is always attachment

The logged line stays `[relay] feedback send failed id=<id> code=<code>` with `code = error.code.as_str()`
(ETIMEDOUT, ECONNECTION, ESOCKET, EDNS, EAUTH, EENVELOPE, EMESSAGE, ETLS, EPROTOCOL). The connection and greeting
timeouts are `FEEDBACK_DEFAULTS.smtpTimeoutMs` (15000): set `MailConfig::timeout` from the feedback options.
